parts.body:
NY Reg 62 limits exclusions to listed categories. Those common in disability income policies include:

- war or act of war (declared or undeclared); service in the armed forces;
- participation in a felony, riot or insurrection;
- suicide, attempted suicide or intentionally self-inflicted injury;
- aviation other than as a fare-paying passenger on a scheduled or charter flight operated by a scheduled airline;
- disabilities from a preexisting condition, within the limits the law allows.

Ordinary sicknesses and injuries outside these categories are not permissible exclusions.

Group disability plans are issued to an employer under a master policy. Compared with individual policies, group plans typically:

- are underwritten on the **group as a whole**, usually without individual medical exams;
- cost **less per unit** of coverage;
- **offset** (integrate) benefits with Social Security and other income;
- end when **employment ends** (individual policies stay with the insured).

Commonly, when the employer pays the premium, benefits are taxable income to the employee; when an individual pays premiums personally with after-tax money, benefits are generally received tax-free.
